meta {
  name: Get section
  type: http
  seq: 9
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sections/{{sectionId}}
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  X-School-Id: {{schoolCode}}
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.id: eq {{sectionId}}
  res.body.code: eq 6-A
  res.body.edges.grade_level.code: eq G6
  res.body.edges.branch.code: eq MAIN
}

docs {
  The single-row read joins the grade level, the branch and the session, so a
  timetable screen needs one call rather than four. The list at 05/08 joins
  fewer: it is read a page at a time and the joins would multiply.

  Sections have no breadth key -- SectionsRead is read/write/delete, with no
  *_all beside it -- because a section is school-wide reference data with
  nobody to narrow it to. So this read is not scoped per caller: whoever may
  read sections reads any of them, and an unknown id is simply 404.

  Where a row IS narrowed, as an enrolment is at 05/14, the miss is 404 as
  well and never 403. A 403 would confirm the row exists, and probing by id is
  the attack the narrowing is there to stop.
}
